From 6d69df540bcd121295723e64fe32bc297a509dde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Maestro <jjmaestro@ieee.org>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:52:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch: keep the environment CC in the configure probes

Four configure probes, for libpq, OGR, wagyu and flatgeobuf, discard the
compiler `AC_PROG_CC` resolved and substitute `pg_config --cc`, on the reasoning
that an extension should be compiled the way the server was. That reasoning
needs the recorded compiler to still be executable wherever PostGIS is built,
and the recorded value is only ever a string in the installed
`Makefile.global`.

It stops holding as soon as PostgreSQL is compiled through a wrapper in a build
tree that no longer exists at extension-build time, which is what a sandboxed
build produces: `pg_config --cc` then names a path that cannot be executed,
every probe exits 127 with "not found", and configure concludes libpq and the
C++ dependencies are all missing. The failure is silent in the sense that
matters, since a probe reports absence and not the reason for it.

Keep `$CC` for these four sites. Being past `AC_PROG_CC`, it is always set, and
it is the compiler the rest of the build uses, so nothing is left undefined.
A build whose `CC` is the same compiler PostgreSQL used, by a path that
resolves, is served correctly; the case that changes behaviour is the one that
was failing outright.

The same four sites exist in `configure.ac`, which regenerating configure would
have to carry.
---
 configure | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 0083173..020c08b 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -17606,7 +17606,7 @@ fi
   LIBS="$PGSQL_FE_LDFLAGS"
 
   CC_SAVE="$CC"
-  CC=`"$PG_CONFIG" --cc`
+  CC="$CC"
 
   CFLAGS_SAVE="$CFLAGS"
   CFLAGS=`"$PG_CONFIG" --cflags`
@@ -23499,7 +23499,7 @@ printf "%s\n" "$OGR_ENABLED" >&6; }
 
 		if test "x$PG_CONFIG" != "xno"; then
 			CFLAGS=`"$PG_CONFIG" --cflags`
-			CC=`"$PG_CONFIG" --cc`
+			CC="$CC"
 		fi
 
 		LIBS_SAVE="$LIBS"
@@ -23737,7 +23737,7 @@ if test "x$HAVE_PROTOBUF" = "xyes"; then
     LDFLAGS_SAVE="$LDFLAGS"
     LIBS_SAVE="$LIBS"
 
-    WAGYU_CXX=`"$PG_CONFIG" --cc`
+    WAGYU_CXX="$CC"
     CPPFLAGS="-x c++"
     CFLAGS=""
     LDFLAGS=""
@@ -28548,7 +28548,7 @@ CPPFLAGS_SAVE="$CPPFLAGS"
 LDFLAGS_SAVE="$LDFLAGS"
 LIBS_SAVE="$LIBS"
 
-FLATGEOBUF_CXX=`"$PG_CONFIG" --cc`
+FLATGEOBUF_CXX="$CC"
 CPPFLAGS="-x c++"
 CFLAGS=""
 LDFLAGS=""
